========================================================================
2. Runtimes and base images
========================================================================

- Java runtime in the distribution tar (runtime/) and in the container image:
  a jlink image of Eclipse Temurin (OpenJDK) 21 - GNU GPL 2.0 with the
  Classpath Exception. The -all.jar download carries no Java runtime.
- Native executables (the -native release file and image, and the prover
  downloads for each system) are built with GraalVM Community native-image
  and contain its Substrate VM runtime and the JDK class library - GNU GPL
  2.0 with the Classpath Exception
- Container images are built on the ubuntu:24.04 base image; its packages
  keep their own licenses (see /usr/share/doc/*/copyright in the image)
- Windows prover downloads carry the llvm-mingw runtime of the wallet's
  native library (see wallet/NOTICE)

========================================================================
3. Deployment files (referenced, not redistributed)
========================================================================

- Caddy (compose.yaml pulls the caddy:2 image; deploy/caddy/Caddyfile) -
  Apache License 2.0
- Cloudflare deployment (deploy/cloudflare): @cloudflare/containers,
  wrangler and @cloudflare/workers-types - MIT or Apache License 2.0;
  TypeScript - Apache License 2.0. They are installed by npm at deploy time.

========================================================================
4. Downloaded at run time (not embedded)
========================================================================

- zkTLS template packs are downloaded from the wallet project's releases and
  verified against the public keys pinned in the wallet's core.
- With bonds_age_verify the server downloads the openac-age-v1 assets (Bonds
  R1CS and keys, compiled from zkID circuits and circomlib templates). They
  are distributed separately under GPL-3.0 and are not linked into the
  server; see wallet/NOTICE for the corresponding source.
- The zkPassport prover downloads the BN254 CRS (the public Aztec Ignition
  ceremony transcript prefix) and the registry data and circuit artifacts
  the zkPassport project publishes.

